<p><strong>A waiting list works when you record who wants a slot, see a cancelled slot the moment it opens, and offer it to the next person quickly. Without that, a full diary still loses customers and a cancelled slot stays empty.</strong></p>
<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>The cancellation at 3 pm</h2>
<p>Saturday is fully booked. A customer asks for a 5 pm massage and is told no. At 3 pm another customer cancels. Nobody remembers who asked, the slot goes empty, and the first customer has already booked somewhere else.</p>
<h2>Why waiting lists fail</h2>
<ul><li><strong>The list lives in someone's head</strong> or on a scrap of paper.</li><li><strong>Nobody sees the cancellation</strong> until the slot has already passed.</li><li><strong>No rule for who gets the slot first.</strong></li></ul>
<h2>A simple waiting list that works</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Write down every request:</strong> name, phone, service, preferred staff member and times they can come.</li><li><strong>Decide the order:</strong> usually first asked, first offered, unless the slot needs a specific skill.</li><li><strong>Offer fast and give a deadline,</strong> for example "reply within 15 minutes".</li><li><strong>Move on if there is no reply,</strong> then try walk-ins and recent customers.</li></ol>
<h2>What Zennly gives you today</h2>
<p>With <a href="/features/booking/">Zennly's live schedule</a>, bookings that are created, rescheduled or cancelled update straight away across branches, so staff see an open slot the moment it appears. Every booking holds the staff member and the real length of the session, so a gap on the schedule is a real gap. <strong>Walk-ins are fitted into those open gaps</strong>, which makes them the second-best way to fill a late cancellation. Customers who book online can only choose free slots. Zennly also has a waiting list, so requests are kept next to the schedule instead of on a scrap of paper.</p>
<h2>Fill the gap after the waiting list</h2>
<p>If nobody on the list can come, message recent customers. <a href="/features/outreach/">Customer outreach</a> sends messages by email, and SMS and WhatsApp are available on request. See how <a href="/solutions/barbershop/">barbershops fit walk-ins into real gaps</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Keep one waiting list sheet at the front desk and in the manager's phone.</li><li>Check the schedule for cancellations every hour on busy days.</li><li>Confirm bookings the day before, so cancellations come early.</li></ol>
